  "description": "Light makes right. So say the grimpeurs and the KOM hunters. Engineered by experts and crafted by the world’s best framebuilders, the Coll dels Reis makes the high mountains your hunting ground. If there’s one thing better than floating up a long climb, it’s being the first to attack the descent… solo. No grade is too steep. No pain is too great. When the mountains are calling, the Coll dels Reis is the answer. The Coll dels Reis is the world's lightest titanium disc-brake road bike, built for riders who live to conquer the highest mountains. With unmatched ride quality and poise, it epitomizes the finest attributes of a true climber's bike. Frame weight: 948-1,049 grams* (size medium) 6.5 kg / 14 lb 6 oz complete bike weight (size medium) Recommended 85 kg / 187 lb rider weight limit Superform FW 3AL/2.5V titanium tubeset Full Integration (FI) hides brake housing, cables, and wiring Threaded BSA - OR- T47i bottom bracket Universal Derailleur Hanger (UDH) -OR- SL Ti dropouts Maximum tire size: 35mm** Shimano Di2 or SRAM eTap AXS-specific design Proudly handcrafted in Chattanooga, TN, using globally sourced premium materials *Lightest configuration uses BSA bottom bracket, Litespeed SL Ti dropouts, and anodized headbadge graphic **Varies based on tire brand, tread, wheel, and fork combination.",
